   "cite": "the-pressure-phase-diagram",
   "prompt": "<p>Suppose $\\kPcircone = 50$ Torr and $\\kPcirctwo = 25$ Torr. If $\\kchione= 0.6$ what is the composition of the vapor?</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "number",
    "value": 0.75,
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "hint": "Find the total pressure from the liquid line first, then use Dalton's law for component 1.",
    "solution": "<p>The liquid line (24.1.4) gives the total pressure: $\\kPtotal = \\kPcirctwo - \\kchione(\\kPcirctwo - \\kPcircone) = 25 - 0.6\\,(25 - 50) = 40$ Torr. By Raoult's law component 1 contributes $\\kPone = \\kchione\\kPcircone = 0.6 \\times 50 = 30$ Torr, so (24.1.5) gives $y_1 = 30/40 = 0.75$ and $y_2 = 0.25$. The vapor holds more of component 1, the more volatile one, than the liquid does (0.6).</p>"
   }
  }
 ],
